    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0606" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg566"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1552.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 29, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 14th instant, (No. 1044,) in regard to the visit of the ex-Queen
                    of the Sandwich Islands to England.</p>
                <p>While approving your vigilance in the matter, I have to request that you will
                    exercise your own discretion as to making suggestions to the effect that we
                    would not look with satisfaction upon any special change in the attitude of the
                    Hawaiian kingdom affecting its relations to the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
